<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $4.9 bln in Nov 18 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $4.9 bln in Nov 18 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $4.9 billion in the November 18 week to $3,796.9 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $12.8 billion to $4,853.0 billion. M-1 rose $7.1 billion to $1,075.6 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,790.2 billion versus $3,785.5 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
